---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import '../styles/prose.css';
import avatar from '../assets/avatar.png';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About — ${site.name}`}
  description="Jason Yang is a protocol engineer at Solstice Labs, building Solana programs and Rust services after a decade in financial products at JPMorgan and HSBC."
>
  <main id="main-content" class="page container about-page" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <div class="avatar-ring">
        <Image
          class="avatar intro-avatar"
          src={avatar}
          alt={`Portrait of ${site.name}`}
          width={96}
          height={96}
          densities={[1, 2]}
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="intro-copy">
        <div class="status-pill"><span class="status-dot"></span>{site.status}</div>
        <h1 id="about-heading" class="display">Hi, I’m Jason.</h1>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="article-prose about-prose">
      <p>
        I’m a Rust engineer at Solstice Labs, based in the UK. I design and build Solana programs in
        Rust and the backend services that keep them running. Before engineering I spent a decade in
        financial products at JPMorgan and HSBC, which still shapes how I think about the systems I
        build: the hard part is usually deciding how a financial system should behave and how to
        secure it, not just how to implement it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-i-do">What I do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Design and implement Solana programs in Rust and Anchor: a stablecoin, a yield vault and a
          tranching platform, taken from financial concept through external audits to mainnet.
        </li>
        <li>
          Build and operate the Rust services around them: protocol APIs, indexing, price feeds,
          automated yield distribution and monitoring.
        </li>
        <li>
          Write the specifications, accounting models and threat models before the code, and the
          property-based tests after it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="background">Background</h2>
      <p>
        Before Solstice I was a Senior Vice President in product development at JPMorgan Chase,
        owning the financial rules for a launched credit card product, and spent nine years at HSBC
        in global cards product management and business planning. I hold a Master’s in Finance from
        The University of Manchester and a Bachelor’s in Finance from Sun Yat-sen University.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-i-work-with">What I work with</h2>
      <p>
        Rust day to day, occasionally Typescript and Python, with PostgreSQL and gRPC on the backend
        and Solana and Anchor on chain.
      </p>

      <h2 id="this-site">This site</h2>
      <p>
        I use small Rust experiments to work through ideas and write up what I learn. Most posts are
        about Rust internals, systems programming and the mechanics behind financial protocols.
      </p>

      <h2 id="get-in-touch">Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={site.linkedin} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a> is the best place
        to start a conversation. My code is on
        <a href={site.github} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
